(Bug #64: the `the` spelling knew `length`, `size` and `empty` but not
 `first`, `last`, `keys`, `values` or a map key, so half a collection's
 documented surface was a parse error behind the article. Every List
 Properties and Map Properties row, read through `the`.)

a list called names is ["Alice", "Bob", "Charlie"].

Print "length: {the names's length}".
Print "size: {the names's size}".
Print "empty: {the names's empty}".
Print "first: {the names's first}".
Print "last: {the names's last}".

a list called 'no names' is [].
Print "empty list: {the 'no names''s empty}".

a map called person is {"name": "Alice", "age": 30}.

Print "keys: {the person's keys}".
Print "values: {the person's values}".
a text called who is the person's "name".
Print "by key: {who}".
Print "map size: {the person's size}".
Print "map empty: {the person's empty}".

(A quoted name is the same name, so the article reads it the same way.)
a list called 'the guest list' is ["Dana", "Eli"].
Print "quoted first: {the 'the guest list''s first}".
Print "quoted last: {the 'the guest list''s last}".
